Cathinka Tandberg: =E2=80=98Spurs fans hate Arsenal. That=E2=80=99s how it =
is=E2=80=99


Norwegian forward might look to Harry Kane for inspiration on the pitch, bu=
t when north London derby comes around, she needs no lessons on what the ri=
valry means


Cathinka Tandberg celebrates scoring against Aston Villa this season. Photo=
graph: Richard Pelham/Getty Images


Sophie Downey


=E2=80=9CIt means more than just three points. It=E2=80=99s for the whole c=
lub. It=E2=80=99s for the whole place. It=E2=80=99s for the whole of Totten=
ham.=E2=80=9D One only needs to be in the presence of Tottenham Cathinka Ta=
ndberg for a few minutes to feel the passion that emanates from her when it=
 comes to this weekend=E2=80=99s north London derby. As a lifelong Spurs fa=
n, the forward understands more than most the intensity of the rivalry that=
 exists between her side and Arsenal, one that she cannot wait to experienc=
e once again on Saturday.

=E2=80=9CIt will just be an incredible feeling,=E2=80=9D she tells Moving t=
he Goalposts. =E2=80=9CI think you will feel a few nerves that you maybe do=
n=E2=80=99t feel in a normal game but that=E2=80=99s good.

=E2=80=9CAll the Spurs fans hate Arsenal and Arsenal hate Spurs. That=E2=80=
=99s how it is. You want to show that you=E2=80=99re the best team =E2=80=
=93 simple as that. You just want to fight for the club, the badge and for =
the people around you.=E2=80=9D


Cathinka Tandberg joined Tottenham from the Swedish side Hammarby in the su=
mmer of 2025. Photograph: Javier Garc=C3=ADa/Tottenham Hotspur FC/Shutterst=
ock


It has been a significant 13 months for the 22-year-old who made her dream =
move to London in September 2025. After catching the eye as a goalscorer in=
 the Damallsvenskan at first Link=C3=B6ping and then Hammarby, the Norwegia=
n was signed by Martin Ho on deadline day to bolster the team=E2=80=99s att=
acking options. She made her mark on her first start,
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECoBtcQjat6FvTX4oDJNDqNVSET1bZh05Qs4nJvc3AZYE6WrO7_p3B_wGo=
fMJnOZVMkhAk_f9lZmA-pUVO1DUaccymDdwWVfhSPzZfZ5SHDocsgRYrW3k3573SUBRyh3SMOTz=
FgE0z1TZIDwSlIdwuVnkxWS-5_hM9PGhhlUOPbtYzzxSYt_Ap_8wEsZTGugdMyXcKdZ69oWpIfR=
6un6XUDTEjMqwVBXAYdzGzByJYPeeObtJWtQNTh6iZ9i8bxGZoDNPB_Ahowwz1aPntfDgp0/4v7=
/k0jm-auyQsWt5v3rbvQ-Ew/t0/h001.R4RuwMv70770vU4E1oXBmVMCOhEHoM3kSWjiUViBA08
scoring a spectacular 40-yard goal
at Everton.

=E2=80=9CI settled really well,=E2=80=9D she reflects. =E2=80=9CI=E2=80=99m=
 really enjoying it and want to push myself forward. It=E2=80=99s been a to=
ugh start [to this season] and I haven=E2=80=99t really got what I wanted. =
But there=E2=80=99s loads of games left. I=E2=80=99m still young. I=E2=80=
=99m still improving and learning. I just have to trust the process and tru=
st what I=E2=80=99m surrounded by.

=E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s a big difference from Sweden,=E2=80=9D she continues.=
 =E2=80=9CYou meet World Cup players week in, week out, so you have to perf=
orm every week if you want results. I feel like my physicality has changed =
a lot. I=E2=80=99ve got stronger and fitter. Playing under Martin has made =
me think more away from the goals. I think more about how I play with the b=
all, how I press and all of those things that I maybe didn=E2=80=99t focus =
on before =E2=80=A6 it=E2=80=99s a bit like Harry Kane. The older he gets, =
he has developed his game as well. He needed to be deeper in the pitch beca=
use that=E2=80=99s how they wanted to play and then he has to be better wit=
h the ball. That=E2=80=99s a bit how I also need to be. I can=E2=80=99t onl=
y just stand in the box. I need to be good everywhere else.=E2=80=9D

Spurs have been
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECoBtcQjat6FvTX4oDJNDqNtq0zuDdy0zgI_bXukqxsMAeWCSkcLH1MmLg=
3gNBThcAf3ESXheuwNjjY2zwhCrJJPi0Z0dA5uBseTdkPJf5VAnqbwd-fbll5p1QrIdUh7plONb=
W_s0N85Q5LcytEkDZTpMHtRGck405taEQ3wmvTDw7duH3kv38W02FnY9Rd13hEXSmJPIcwOiBjH=
zanGItoTJDOTLB90CEMvEHhXrOaVjDU5WWzWfHKmnlxQSW58IBFObLVadbJGDrJ-utf6Y4--c9C=
-S5jULnz2saeOLD994juQYvlb27SJ2pNwQoltlE/4v7/k0jm-auyQsWt5v3rbvQ-Ew/t1/h001.=
MpNcablrroFBfDNB4hoHahsI4XsN6J5usS5W35yeRI8
transformed under Ho
and finished fifth last season. However, with success
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgw9f1pffWfnUSsO_-0q10D9u9BgZeOeaaz4_=
BQlUg34PQ7wIoSFs4L9AsOfhO_6rhMgUkSK9O0jM3ueogKU4BmOF271SoNwjpWkkRqffNGCkWf8=
Hv57VSdRGTxfFqFjyY6wuQzkXLwvzDuzjrzoKqqH3W75hyTrqk5RM__NLkn_3Lu11kEoMMjvvQX=
_FcUlNBHggMCMJShaJCT-_5FWDSH-rc0yNHH8tLSwlwRZBJ5WGf-eXjnZn7HbR9xcJBOyYw54yu=
xjD3oAeuvQ4Vg3vDqQ/4v7/k0jm-auyQsWt5v3rbvQ-Ew/t2/h001.MxJwpTtkfjwhP6JhuDxwE=
dd3viR7xRpkzmd4yjVF5WQ
comes expectation
, ambitions that Tandberg clearly shares but with a sense of perspective.

=E2=80=9CTottenham has always been a Champions League club for me,=E2=80=9D=
 she says. =E2=80=9CBut I=E2=80=99m a fan so I can=E2=80=99t really talk fo=
r the other players. When I came to the club, I said that I want to get top=
 three. But you also need to be realistic and to see where the team has bee=
n before. The transformation that Martin has done in a season is unbelievab=
le. I don=E2=80=99t think anyone else could do that. That tells you everyth=
ing about him. He=E2=80=99s one of the greatest coaches I=E2=80=99ve worked=
 with and I think everyone that comes here, one of the reasons is because o=
f him. We all trust him and the process.=E2=80=9D


=E2=80=98Tottenham has always been a Champions League club for me. But I=E2=
=80=99m a fan so I can=E2=80=99t really talk for the other players. When I =
came to the club, I said that I want to get top three. But you also need to=
 be realistic and to see where the team has been before.=E2=80=99 Cathinka =
Tandberg=E2=80=99s ambitions for her club are high. Photograph: Leila Coker=
/WSL Football/Getty Images


That faith is currently being tested. After an unbeaten start, Tottenham ha=
ve suffered back-to-back defeats, conceding six goals to both London City L=
ionesses
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgCgwaDyJ7Figpee1BMqRVH5xsIHLzli053ta=
YNtGjAHBrn7AlZy0igPL-taSgigUQtO720dxsQY5JPj1jzG6T6opY5R0fohC5l6Jv1Y1J2FqExf=
mTBo_vRCOBYWGmYbeR-pCTUG0csx2SSU38fQ2cqXz1WvhRmvippdUYafOrKV_Ap95vIQ8KtnQ8i=
d2CJAFMAxKAQsCAO2a-EJHcN-IYMU_y7h8olrx2iRuo76-RUf7e2WuHzLxL1d2HkXWiw1cC/4v7=
/k0jm-auyQsWt5v3rbvQ-Ew/t3/h001.ydhLykqWi-yBmM3w5dMMULYUy8eI819QRZv6GJRl2bE
and Chelsea
.

=E2=80=9CYou can call it a dip in form but I still feel like we also showed=
 our qualities in those games,=E2=80=9D Tandberg says. =E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99=
s just about ourselves. We maybe need to change our mentality a bit, find t=
hat fire and dig a bit deeper when we play those top teams. I feel like may=
be it=E2=80=99s good that it=E2=80=99s come because it had to at some point=
. It=E2=80=99s about how we respond.

=E2=80=9CWe also have to realise where this team has been. Two years ago, i=
t was a relegation club. We need to realise how quickly it has [changed]. B=
ut, of course, we have expectations and levels that we want to come to and =
we know that we can. I feel like we=E2=80=99re working so well =E2=80=A6 we=
 just have to believe in everyone.=E2=80=9D

For Tandberg, putting that right against a struggling Arsenal in front of a=
 home crowd would be the perfect tonic. =E2=80=9CI=E2=80=99ve always been a=
 passionate player and I=E2=80=99ve been a supporter,=E2=80=9D she says. =
=E2=80=9CI play for the supporters because I just enjoy it and I know how i=
t is to be in the stands. I think [that connection] is very important becau=
se we have their back and they have ours. To give them something back is im=
portant and to show that we see and hear them every time.=E2=80=9D

