<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">And so here we are again, at that point as=
 the nights draw in and Manchester United <a href=3D"https://ablink.editori=
al.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtj=
hYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPg4Po31vrjVzXiEA_Xskplj7xNfI1oLzZpgNfjxuNWdsj0Bhrehr8iI6bEA=
gUzs7Z2RRFQ-nU36PSMEeeGueWvTPmBnIrqJnrQ5OsZj2ee0YFviCZrzzQi4jyz3oHalTVEb9ia=
Imz-OuVdF7boTqdhkP8Ts1VRrkhPXSa36x_kbilVBwLJbf_LeKF8cmKkDI7n6qdnHNmHDg9YXcO=
R5wbAo7Y8KiGREBieItevRDiCTeLONN_3DjpYMjGGl4ERUGWn0hYiBkjLvttxEFnbjtLIlVLH2n=
GdaJ7DVdxfWrfgi8-Q05k22EdwfwGYACn5KADD-xN1h1Rp8a4IGImBtq7xxA/4v7/k0jm-auyQs=
Wt5v3rbvQ-Ew/h9/h001.DmxdLsfxvhFpUzxdk4wouVF0PEJVjaRvZxptnyf0VNo" style=3D"=
color: #0077B6;">prepare to sack a manager</a>. Autumn: season of mists, me=
llow fruitfulness and a crisis at Old Trafford. <a href=3D"https://ablink.e=
ditorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSne=
HEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPg4Po31vrjVzXiEA_Xskplj7YpQ91av02pZpcavv2h3OkgHY5xs3r=
bSparv0WMX_C-GQirgBnEKDz7kMJMBUF8FOxtY-CcJkRKItWCG0pYhdoVMhMcgQs4iWVGuospMA=
cksMwlzQsQR1THm9BBSZwLD4JWye0rBrw7nF9UljUP1bOhXSsAldHR1pLbLUqJ1XSML3Y0VbL-T=
cfPhw9Ax7J9QugejYcSWrezgs8VqgcDsUggxkNQXAjxtz8VuIXB8Gn3tmrMmHXckeY6z_rTwzdw=
Fh6gYeHuhdvio4v_YvB17FAkSXZIz-0hdCfnMIO3U2QD/4v7/k0jm-auyQsWt5v3rbvQ-Ew/h10=
/h001.CVps_c5bISwmw1DPp50r_iBVOy0hDSGrMJ47xTaXgik" style=3D"color: #0077B6;=
">Sunday=E2=80=99s 3-0 home defeat to Bournemouth</a>, coming on the back o=
f last week=E2=80=99s 4-1 reverse against Como, made clear what many had fe=
ared from the moment Michael Carrick was given the job on a permanent basis=
: that he isn=E2=80=99t up to it.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">But then, who could be? When you=E2=80=99v=
e burned through a long list of managers in 13 years, it=E2=80=99s perhaps =
worth considering whether the manager is really the problem. Could some bla=
me perhaps go to the director of football, Jason Wilcox, or the chief execu=
tive, Omar Berrada, the people making the appointments? Or perhaps to Sir J=
im Ratcliffe, the cost-cutting tax exile and minority shareholder with resp=
onsibility for sporting operations? Or to the Glazer family, who plunged th=
e club into debt with a leveraged buyout in 2005 and have since made calami=
tous decision after calamitous decision, reducing the most successful club =
in English league history to a mid-table laughing stock with a roof <a href=
=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18I=
RyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECOCDTrc8QlvRqgzQLHrqJM-IRstHm-4717JFo_4YWUY1StKPXQs2t=
GHpeSsS1hJOeUfaZvuVBJMYGlUSkY516VoMimAnLPapMFpU8DhTgCLc7icbXX5yuzG44aND7yrV=
rMmkq4_fe-_3AsYnaI0C737mQyrPp2R6KsmiefVBDMhq-uB1kuvGt66sfKGOiTYUJ6sPHq1pA2-=
azKf2SieX5Wu7Rxfg_afRmGmcI_4rJofQx_qnTvgFxNdrPsc2Zoy3sU9tAox0bG7rDoS7LotltA=
mSdG89tnxKcsZ0kG4keNv6iPfpaWN3rYa7a1i0OxjLHqRljTlyV0bfEi6MicAwEx/4v7/k0jm-a=
uyQsWt5v3rbvQ-Ew/h11/h001.yuM-a7opZahxoDR9LpLeb4R2VSjq1J6MlTcp71rJR48" styl=
e=3D"color: #0077B6;">that leaks symbolically</a>?</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It=E2=80=99s worth remembering where all t=
his began. The United story has taken on the aspect of a classical tragedy =
and, like all good tragedies, it begins with a small, seemingly unconnected=
 moment, amplified by pride, that ends up bringing the whole edifice crashi=
ng down.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In 1999, Mull of Kintyre, a horse owned by=
 the Irish millionaire John Magnier, won the Gimcrack Stakes at York. Tradi=
tionally, the winning owner would give a speech at the Gimcrack Dinner, but=
 Magnier was a shy man who hated public speaking so he asked his friend, th=
e United manager Alex Ferguson, to give the speech on his behalf. The racin=
g establishment, though, refused: it had to be the owner. To spite them, Ma=
gnier named Ferguson as the owner of another horse, Juniper. The following =
year, Juniper was narrowly beaten in the Gimcrack Stakes. Magnier, though, =
was determined. So the year after that, he made Ferguson the owner of Rock =
of Gibraltar, which had won its first three races. Rock of Gibraltar won th=
e Gimcrack easily and Magnier, waving a metaphorical two fingers at the rac=
ing authorities, watched Ferguson give the speech.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Magnier was largely making mischief, but h=
e was also happy to do a favor for a friend, to give Ferguson a better expe=
rience of racing, and he benefited from the association of the horse with s=
uch a famous name. In addition, Ferguson did not get on well with the Unite=
d chairman, Martin Edwards, and had a sense that football clubs were becomi=
ng good investments. Accordingly Magnier and his associate JP McManus bough=
t shares in United. (The full story <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.the=
guardian.com/ss/c/u001.HT6_61rcAeQ71YMHfBFwudh8nG4NaBrfCAiRj3N5vPU0dA6ArLsE=
JD9i6Km11Dj55cD2iWkYKFmR_D9L13wO9L_X7KurHGB8krj5G6sGbpxcAXMk977dYNmxleLH_bk=
4Ivm4wNW_azma-o4GwxSDfmxNtCPfSbwFpHbvF1OEwTYDubynrg8sKmwxIY2r7NBDq0X72XEcmz=
Q8W-uzKaE4zWCbpIOzZOkXFilsmDPG2gxSeSCLDU_TRbLsH2UQBCYX_w7GSWlhONa1iVd8LGBer=
jfLp-7n2e8ICR7mOChovQdp88gs2X8EAN_6mGR2aLAPbs3KGNAPtBlvH32BvFyigQQM-uJUlXmU=
rFciIUTYcRU/4v7/k0jm-auyQsWt5v3rbvQ-Ew/h12/h001.qQ3ga-l-dSDBdKUvaI5Wl2El20Y=
hpGbmdYZJaKFxyUc" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">is explored by the journalist D=
avid Walsh here</a>).</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It turned out, though, that Rock of Gibral=
tar was a much better horse than anybody had realized, winning seven Group =
One races in a row. The stud fees would be worth tens of millions of pounds=
. Ferguson believed the verbal deal was that he could choose 50% of the pri=
ze money won by Rock of Gibraltar (about =C2=A3800,000) or 50% of the stud =
fees, which ended up being worth tens of millions. He went for the latter. =
Magnier=E2=80=99s recollection was rather different: 5% of the prize money =
or one stud nomination a year.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Ferguson sued and, with his name on the ow=
nership documents, probably would have won had it gone to trial. But then r=
umors started to spread about some of Ferguson=E2=80=99s financial dealings=
 at United. Paid actors at United=E2=80=99s annual general meeting raised a=
wkward points, then Magnier and McManus sent a list of 99 questions to the =
United board, which mysteriously found their way into the Daily Mail. Unite=
d were highly embarrassed. Fans began to demonstrate against Magnier and Mc=
Manus at race meetings. A settlement was reached, with Ferguson paid =C2=A3=
2.5m to drop the action. But the damage was done.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Magnier and McManus had decided to sell th=
eir shares in United, and another shareholder was ready and waiting: Malcol=
m Glazer. Ferguson backed Glazer, who launched his leveraged buyout. Magnie=
r and McManus sold up in 2005 for =C2=A3260m, a profit of a little under =
=C2=A3100m. Had they waited for Ratcliffe, who bought a similar stake in 20=
24, they would have received roughly =C2=A31bn more than that. For Ferguson=
, a threat had been dealt with.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The problem was that Glazer and his family=
 would prove <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.=
Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBYsb93GJSEF_C1-UhtUYc3CyHiQTM32B4=
wGDdedcWnsQjPH0zR7uzoCmRQa_NZFRumw5dGfMR7mTl0_gjbPeyDfgXmRejbEd_bv7o_3eVFpl=
-iSXPkqYk_D_VWJZNOtpFcIm5WTvtAO121pKo5HuzHBjdjI_NZJG-YnNDIDWre70SVMuQDMQ4YJ=
L9dX9HIbMgN-KfKzPBBWjS7d0yf7-8USfDAfabWDOl-W4bi9SwIWttbARLitJ2dFKy8vyKwNUzB=
u7Jj1qFQvVRYF56adMfeI2EnDxc62nZjLgUCOUdjWDYLagC7zb7GiwKh99mCUhGrPoAWJ5u8ESb=
4HxG3M4o_/4v7/k0jm-auyQsWt5v3rbvQ-Ew/h13/h001.bBowBA2hYksyKR6HJ84HMtX56LAo1=
STiRveojaQUioc" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">some of the worst club owners</a>=
 in English history. For 20 years, United have been addled by debt and have=
 made consistently terrible footballing decisions. Ferguson=E2=80=99s team =
was good enough, and his personality big enough, that United won five leagu=
e titles and a Champions League after the takeover, but once his genius had=
 gone, there was nothing left.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A mismatched squad built up over seven fla=
wed managerial appointments and a multiplicity of conflicting approaches wi=
ll not readily be sorted out. Carrick is the latest victim of a crisis 21 y=
ears in the making. For the want of a horse a club was lost.</p>
